This is a simple and rather powerful demonstration of the associative property of real numbers. Considering left-hand side of equation:

$$42 + x^4 + x^2 + x^3 < 43$$

Observe, we can switch variables in above expression considering index (Power) of variable x, by exchanging x with power of x, which can be rewritten in integer as:

$$42 + x^x\cdot x^2\cdot x^3 < 43$$

where, k⋅l=m

or the above can be further rewritten as:

$$42 + x^{x+2+3} < 42+1$$

Now we have:  <p style="text-align:center;">42 < N<|N(x) - D(x)|<|dN(x)|<|D(x)|=1</

To solve this, we first transpose the $4x$ from LHS to RHS and the $+7$ from RHS to LHS, \begin{align*}
4x+5 &= 6x+7 \\
&= \mathbf{4x+5-4x-5} = \mathbf{6x+7-4x-7} \\
0 &= 2x+2\\
-2 &= 2x \\
x&= \boxed{-1}
\end{align*}

